{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/publications/east-region-firing-times/fingringhoe-and-barton-road-eata-may-2026-firing-times","content_id":"ddab27a0-1f06-4f23-abbd-cc45515ce25b","description":null,"details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>As seen in the Security Defence Review, the Army is at heightened readiness due to a new era of threat. This has placed greater demands on the Defence Training Estate (DTE) across the UK, which is being used for training more regularly and at shorter notice.</p>\n\n<p>As such, the firing time notifications published on Gov.UK have been standardised to show the daily timings for when live-firing is permitted on the UK DTE. This is a change from the previous method of showing when training bookings had been made in advance.</p>\n\n<p>This to ensure safety of all users, as it is not possible to change Gov.UK notifications at short notice. Broadly, the only guaranteed safe times for access are before or after the firing times provided on this page, however there may be exceptional circumstances where extensions have been requested.</p>\n\n<p>If you wish to use the DTE for recreation, please always refer to onsite safety warning signals to understand if the site is safe to access before doing so.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"firing-times-for-november-2026\">Firing times for November 2026:</h2>\n\n<p>These are the standard firing times subject to operational requirement extensions:</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"fingringhoe-and-barton-road\">Fingringhoe and Barton Road</h3>\n\n<table>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Monday:</td>\n      <td>No firing</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Tuesday:</td>\n      <td>9am to 3:30pm</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Wednesday:</td>\n      <td>9am to 3:30pm (night firing until 11pm on request)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Thursday:</td>\n      <td>9am to 3:30pm</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Friday:</td>\n      <td>9am to 12:30pm</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Saturday:</td>\n      <td>9am to 3:30pm</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>Sunday:</td>\n      <td>9am to 2pm</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2 id=\"your-safety\">Your safety</h2>\n\n<div class=\"call-to-action\">\n  <p>Danger - when warning signals are displayed, regardless of the timings, do not cross the range boundary.</p>\n\n  <p>Warning signals are red flags by day and red lamps by night; range boundaries are marked by red and white poles.</p>\n\n  <p>Red flags and red lamps indicate that live firing is taking place within the range boundaries.</p>\n\n  <p>Do not enter the danger area when in use, this could result in loss of life.</p>\n\n  <p>Do not touch any military debris, it may be dangerous. Please note the location and inform a Training Safety Officer (TSO) via 07766813725 or the police.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Learn more about <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safe-access\">accessing MOD training areas safely</a> safely.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/public-access-to-military-areas\">Public access to military land</a>.</p>\n\n<p>Please note:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Firing takes place when roads are marked as ‘Closed’</li>\n  <li>There is no entry into the out of bounds area, which is completely fenced and appropriately signed</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"contact-us\">Contact us</h2>\n\n<p>For further information on the armed forces’ training at Fingringhoe &amp; Barton Rd, contact:</p>\n\n<div class=\"address\"><div class=\"adr org fn\"><p>\nEast Anglia Training Area,<br>Fingringhoe Range Complex,<br>Lodge Lane,<br>Langenhoe,<br>Colchester,<br>Essex,<br>CO5 7LX\n</p></div></div>\n\n<p>Email address: DTEOpsRoomEast@landmarc.mod.uk</p>\n\n<p>Phone: 07818 900806 / 07977346026</p>\n</div>","first_published_version":false,"headers":[{"headers":[{"id":"fingringhoe-and-barton-road","level":3,"text":"Fingringhoe and Barton Road"}],"id":"firing-times-for-november-2026","level":2,"text":"Firing times for November 2026:"},{"id":"your-safety","level":2,"text":"Your safety"},{"id":"contact-us","level":2,"text":"Contact us"}],"political":false,"public_timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:31:11.000+00:00"},"document_type":"html_publication","first_published_at":"2026-04-22T16:23:17+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/publications/east-region-firing-times/fingringhoe-and-barton-road-eata-may-2026-firing-times","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/publications/east-region-firing-times/fingringhoe-and-barton-road-eata-may-2026-firing-times","base_path":"/government/publications/east-region-firing-times/fingringhoe-and-barton-road-eata-may-2026-firing-times","content_id":"ddab27a0-1f06-4f23-abbd-cc45515ce25b","document_type":"html_publication","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-10-28T17:31:11Z","schema_name":"html_publication","title":"Fingringhoe and Barton Road (EATA) November 2026 firing times","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/east-region-firing-times/fingringhoe-and-barton-road-eata-may-2026-firing-times","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2015-conservative-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2015-conservative-government","base_path":"/government/2015-conservative-government","content_id":"d4fbc1b9-d47d-4386-af04-ac909f868f92","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2016-07-13T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2015-05-08T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2015 to 2016 Cameron Conservative government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2015-conservative-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","details":{"acronym":"MOD","brand":"ministry-of-defence